  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Current Mobile Toon material shader does not properly shade models, and resembles neither a \"toon\" shader nor provides shading, instead functioning as an \"unlit\" material which merely adjusts its texture's exposure in response to lighting intensity of directional lights. \n \nNot only is this non-functional, but this completely breaks visibility of avatars, using toon materials, viewed atop like colored environments, also using toon materials. This pushes the mobile toon shader into the category of \"a bug\" or otherwise undesired behavior of the VRChat application. \n \nToon shaders should have \"solid\" shading, with a \"hard cut-off\" between lit and unlit areas, as can be seen in the image provided (from Breath of the Wild). \n \nHowever, Mobile Toon provides NO shading at all. As can be seen in the provided \"selfie\", models, which do not provide \"pre-shaded\" textures (e.g center model), experience an \"unshaded\" appearance, with all visual dimensional detail being lost within similarly colored areas (complete left model; right model's body material). \n \nFor example, the *first 2 steps* of https://roystan.net/articles/toon-shader.html provide considerably desirable avatar lighting, and would be an exceptional starting point for a functional toon shader. Optimizations could be made which provide equal performance to Standard Lite, presumably. \n \nAs it stands, Mobile Toon is broken, and non-functioning, as a Quest compatible shader, and feels more like an untested material which was merely \"assumed\" to work.",
